{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>To the chief musician, on Ayelet ha-Shachar</b> — as when one sees the strength of the dawn's rising. And some say: it is the name of a musical instrument. Now we know that [in] יו\"ד איילותי, like גבר, the alef is without a dagesh; therefore it is far-fetched for אילת to be derived from this formation. And the correct interpretation in my eyes: it is the beginning of a piyyut composed in the manner of love-poetry, like אילת אהבים, and this psalm [is set] to the sweetness of its melody."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:28:07.957829496Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}